     "text": "Savage PLC Clinic \nRe: Mark Boyer (DOB 03/02/1988)\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI hope this letter finds you well. I am writing to provide medical information regarding Mr. Mark Boyer, who has been under my care at Savage PLC Clinic. Below is a summary of his relevant medical history and recent visits.\n\nMr. Boyer was diagnosed with BRCA/Lynch syndrome in February 2019. This condition has been controlled, and he underwent surgery to manage the risk factors associated with this diagnosis. \n\n**March 12, 2026**: Mr. Boyer visited our clinic today for follow-up regarding his BRCA/Lynch syndrome, which remains without any cancer development. His blood was recorded at 143/75 mmHg, and his weight was 229 pounds. Upon examination, he was found to be in good with normal findings otherwise. \n\n**January 17, 2025**: Mr. Boyer's follow-up visit on this date concerned his BRCA/Lynch syndrome. His blood pressure was 144/86 mmHg, and his weight was 215 pounds. He was doing well, with no signs of cancer or other complications related to his condition. \n\n**November 25, 2023**: Mr. Boyer visited on this date for continued management of his BRCA/Lynch syndrome. His blood pressure was 143/86 mmHg, and his weight was 221 pounds. He reported no symptoms and was doing well. His prophylactic surgery for BRCA/Lynch syndrome is progressing as expected.\n\n**October 02, 2022**: Mr. Boyer\n"
